{
  "title": "17: Al-Isra الإسراء",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسُبْحٰنَ الَّذِىْۤ اَسْرٰى بِعَبْدِهٖ لَيْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصَا الَّذِىْ بٰرَكْنَا حَوْلَهٗ لِنُرِيَهٗ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(1)\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE ASRAA BE-A’BDEHI LAYLAM MENAL MASJEDIL HARAAME ELAL MASJEDIL AQSAL LAZEE BAARAKNAA HAWLAHU LE-NOREYAHU MIN AAYAATENAA, INNAHU HOWAS SAMEE-U’L BASEER.\nImmaculate is He who carried His servant on a journey by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque whose environs We have blessed, that We might show him some of Our signs. Indeed, He is the All-hearing, the All-seeing.\nوَاٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَ جَعَلْنٰهُ هُدًى لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَلَّا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِىْ وَكِيْلًا ؕ‏(2)\nWA AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LNAAHO HODAL LE-BANEE ISRAAA-EELA ALLAA TATTAKHEZOO MIN DOONEE WAKEELAA.\nWe gave Moses the Book, and made it a guide for the Children of Israel—[saying,] ‘Do not take any trustee besides Me’—\nذُرِّيَّةَ مَنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوْحٍؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَبْدًا شَكُوْرًا‏(3)\nZURRIYYATA MAN HAMALNAA MA-A’ NOOH, INNAHU KAANA A’BDAN SHAKOORAA.\ndescendants of those whom We carried [in the ark] with Noah. Indeed, he was a grateful servant.\nوَقَضَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ فِى الْكِتٰبِ لَتُفْسِدُنَّ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَّتَيْنِ وَلَتَعْلُنَّ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(4)\nWA QAZAYNAA ELAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA FIL KETAABE LATUFSEDUNNA FIL ARZE MARRATAYNE WA LATA’LUNNA O’LUWWAN KABEERAA.\nWe revealed to the Children of Israel in the Book: ‘Twice you will cause corruption on the earth, and you will perpetrate great tyranny.’\nفَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ اُوْلٰٮهُمَا بَعَثْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ عِبَادًا لَّنَاۤ اُولِىْ بَاْسٍ شَدِيْدٍ فَجَاسُوْا خِلٰلَ الدِّيَارِ ؕ وَكَانَ وَعْدًا مَّفْعُوْلًا‏(5)\nFA-EZAA JAAA-A WA’DO OOLAAHOMAA BA-A’SNAA A’LAYKUM E’BAADAL LANAA OOLEE BAASIN SHADEEDIN FA-JAASOO KHELAALAD DEYAAR, WA KAANA WA’DAM MAF-O’OLAA.\nSo when the first occasion of the two [prophecies] came, We aroused against you Our servants possessing great might, and they ransacked [your] habitations, and the promise was bound to be fulfilled.\nثُمَّ رَدَدْنَا لَكُمُ الْكَرَّةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَاَمْدَدْنٰكُمْ بِاَمْوَالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ وَجَعَلْنٰكُمْ اَكْثَرَ نَفِيْرًا‏(6)\nSUMMA RADADNAA LAKOMUL KARRATA A’LAYHIM WA AMDADNAAKUM BE-AMWAALINW WA BANEENA WA JA-A’LNAAKUM AKSARA NAFEERAA.\nThen We gave you back the turn [to prevail] over them, and We aided you with children and wealth, and made you greater in number,\nاِنْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْوَاِنْ اَسَاْتُمْ فَلَهَا ؕ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ الْاٰخِرَةِ لِيَسُوْۤءا وُجُوْهَكُمْ وَلِيَدْخُلُوا الْمَسْجِدَ كَمَا دَخَلُوْهُ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّلِيُتَبِّرُوْا مَا عَلَوْا تَتْبِيْرًا‏(7)\nIN AHSANTUM AHSANTUM LE-ANFOSEKUM, WA IN ASAATUM FALAHAA, FA-EZAA JAAA-A WA’DUL AAKHERATE LE-YASOO-OO WOJOOHAKUM WA LE-YADKHOLUL MASJEDA KAMAA DAKHALOOHO AWWALA MARRATINW WA LE-YOTABBEROO MAA A’LAW TATBEERAA.\n[saying,] ‘If you do good, you will do good to your [own] souls, and if you do evil, it will be [evil] for them.’ So when the occasion for the other [prophecy] comes, they will make your faces wretched, and enter the Temple just as they entered it the first time, and destroy utterly whatever they come upon.\nعَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يَّرْحَمَكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ عُدْتُّمْ عُدْنَاۘ وَجَعَلْنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ حَصِيْرًا‏(8)\nA’SAA RABBOKUM AN-Y YARHAMAKUM, WA IN U’TTUM U’DNAA, WA JA-A’LNAA JAHANNAMA LIL-KAAFEREENA HASEERAA.\nMaybe your Lord will have mercy on you, but if you revert, We [too] will revert, and We have made hell a prison for the faithless.\nاِنَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ يَهْدِىْ لِلَّتِىْ هِىَ اَقْوَمُ وَ يُبَشِّرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ اَنَّ لَهُمْ اَجْرًا كَبِيْرًا ۙ‏(9)\nINNA HAAZAL QUR-AANA YAHDEE LILLATEE HEYA AQWAMO WA YOBASH-SHERUL MOAMENEENAL LAZEENA YA’MALOONAS SAALEHAATE ANNA LAHUM AJRAN KABEERAA.\nIndeed this Quran guides to what is most upright, and gives the good news to the faithful who do righteous deeds that there is a great reward for them.\nوَّاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ اَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا‏(10)\nWA ANNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-AAKHERATE A-A’TADNAA LAHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAs for those who do not believe in the Hereafter, We have prepared a painful punishment for them.\nوَيَدْعُ الْاِنْسَانُ بِالشَّرِّ دُعَآءَهٗ بِالْخَيْرِ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ عَجُوْلًا‏(11)\nWA YAD-U’L INSAANO BISH-SHARRE DO-A’AA-AHU BIL-KHAYR, WA KAANAL INSAANO A’JOOLAA.\nMan prays for ill as [avidly as] he prays for good, and man is overhasty.\nوَجَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ اٰيَتَيْنِ فَمَحَوْنَاۤ اٰيَةَ الَّيْلِ وَجَعَلْنَاۤ اٰيَةَ النَّهَارِ مُبْصِرَةً لِّتَبْتَغُوْا فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَلِتَعْلَمُوْا عَدَدَ السِّنِيْنَ وَالْحِسَابَؕ وَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ فَصَّلْنٰهُ تَفْصِيْلًا‏(12)\nWA JA-A’LNAL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA AAYATAYNE FA-MAHAWNAA AAYATAL LAYLE WA JA-A’LNAA AAYATAN NAHAARE MUBSERATAL LE-TABTAGHOO FAZLAM MIR RABBEKUM WA LE-TA’LAMOO A’DADAS SENEENA WAL HESAAB, WA KULLA SHAY-IN FASSALNAAHO TAFSEELAA.\nWe made the night and the day two signs. Then We faded out the sign of the night, and made the sign of the day lightsome, so that you may seek from your Lord’s bounty and that you may know the number of years and calculation [of time], and We have elaborated everything in detail.\nوَكُلَّ اِنْسَانٍ اَلْزَمْنٰهُ طٰۤئِرَهٗ فِىْ عُنُقِهٖؕ وَنُخْرِجُ لَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ كِتٰبًا يَّلْقٰٮهُ مَنْشُوْرًا‏(13)\nWA KULLA INSAANIN ALZAMNAAHO TAAA-ERAHU FEE O’NOQEH, WA NUKHREJO LAHU YAWMAL QEYAAMATE KETAABAN-Y YALQAAHO MANSHOORAA.\nWe have attached every person’s omen to his neck, and We shall bring it out for him on the Day of Resurrection as a book that he will find wide open.\nاِقْرَاْ كِتٰبَك َؕ كَفٰى بِنَفْسِكَ الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكَ حَسِيْبًا ؕ‏(14)\nIQRAA KETAABAK, KAFAA BE-NAFSEKAL YAWMA A’LAYKA HASEEBAA.\n‘Read your book! Today your soul suffices as your own reckoner.’\nمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖ ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَا ؕ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى ؕ وَمَا كُنَّا مُعَذِّبِيْنَ حَتّٰى نَبْعَثَ رَسُوْلًا‏(15)\nMANEH TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LE-NAFSEH, WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZILLO A’LAYHAA, WA LAA TAZERO WAAZERATUNW WIZRA UKHRAA, WA MAA KUNNAA MO-A’ZZEBEENA HATTAA NAB-A’SA RASOOLAA.\nWhoever is guided is guided only for [the good of] his own soul, and whoever goes astray, goes astray only to its detriment. No bearer shall bear another’s burden. We do not punish [any community] until We have sent [it] an apostle.\nوَاِذَاۤ اَرَدْنَاۤ اَنْ نُّهْلِكَ قَرْيَةً اَمَرْنَا مُتْرَفِيْهَا فَفَسَقُوْا فِيْهَا فَحَقَّ عَلَيْهَا الْقَوْلُ فَدَمَّرْنٰهَا تَدْمِيْرًا‏(16)\nWA EZAA ARADNAA AN NOHLEKA QARYATAN AMARNAA MUTRAFEEHAA FA-FASAQOO FEEHAA FA-HAQQA A’LAYHAL QAWLO FA-DAMMARNAAHAA TADMEERAA.\nAnd when We desire to destroy a town We command its affluent ones [to obey Allah]. But they commit transgression in it, and so the word becomes due against it, and We destroy it utterly.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ نُوْحٍؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(17)\nWA KAM AHLAKNAA MENAL QOROONE MIM BA’DE NOOH, WA KAFAA BE-RABBEKA BE-ZONOOBE E’BAADEHI KHABEERAM BASEERAA.\nHow many generations We have destroyed since Noah! Your Lord is sufficient as [a witness who is] well aware and percipient of His servants’ sins.\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْعَاجِلَةَ عَجَّلْنَا لَهٗ فِيْهَا مَا نَشَآءُ لِمَنْ نُّرِيْدُ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَا لَهٗ جَهَنَّمَۚ يَصْلٰٮهَا مَذْمُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا‏(18)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDUL A’AJELATA A’JJALNAA LAHU FEEHAA MAA NASHAAA-O LEMAN NOREEDO SUMMA JA-A’LNAA LAHU JAHANNAM, YASLAAHAA MAZMOOMAM MADHOORAA.\nWhoever desires this transitory life, We expedite for him therein whatever We wish, for whomever We desire. Then We appoint hell for him, to enter it, blameful and spurned.\nوَمَنْ اَرَادَ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَسَعٰى لَهَا سَعْيَهَا وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ كَانَ سَعْيُهُمْ مَّشْكُوْرًا‏(19)\nWA MAN ARAADAL AAKHERATA WA SA-A’A LAHAA SA’YAHAA WA HOWA MOAMENUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA KAANA SA’YOHUM MASHKOORAA.\nWhoever desires the Hereafter and strives for it with an endeavour worthy of it, should he be faithful,—the endeavour of such will be well-appreciated.\nكُلًّا نُّمِدُّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مِنْ عَطَآءِ رَبِّكَ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ عَطَآءُ رَبِّكَ مَحْظُوْرًا‏(20)\nKULLAN NOMIDDO HAA-OLAAA-E WA HAA-OLAAA-E MIN A’TAAA-E RABBEK, WA MAA KAANA A’TAAA-O RABBEKA MAHZOORAA.\nTo these and to those—to all We extend the bounty of your Lord, and the bounty of your Lord is not confined.\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ ؕ وَلَلْاٰخِرَةُ اَكْبَرُ دَرَجٰتٍ وَّاَكْبَرُ تَفْضِيْلًا‏(21)\nUNZUR KAYFA FAZZALNAA BA’ZAHUM A’LAA BA’Z, WA LAL-AAKHERATO AKBARO DARAJAATINW WA AKBARO TAFZEELAA.\nObserve how We have given some of them an advantage over some others; yet the Hereafter is surely greater in respect of ranks and greater in respect of relative merit.\nلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتَقْعُدَ مَذْمُوْمًا مَّخْذُوْلًا‏(22)\nLAA TAJ-A’L MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA FA-TAQ-O’DA MAZMOOMAM MAKHZOOLAA.\nDo not set up another god besides Allah, or you will sit blameworthy, forsaken.\nوَقَضٰى رَبُّكَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا ؕ اِمَّا يَبْلُغَنَّ عِنْدَكَ الْكِبَرَ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اَوْ كِلٰهُمَا فَلَا تَقُلْ لَّهُمَاۤ اُفٍّ وَّلَا تَنْهَرْهُمَا وَقُلْ لَّهُمَا قَوْلًا كَرِيْمًا‏(23)\nWA QAZAA RABBOKA ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA IYYAAHO WA BIL-WAALEDAYNE EHSAANAA, IMMAA YABLOGHANNA I’NDAKAL KEBARA AHADOHOMAA AW KELAAHOMAA FALAA TAQUL LAHOMAA UFFINW WA LAA TANHARHOMAA WA QUL LAHOMAA QAWLAN KAREEMAA.\nYour Lord has decreed that you shall not worship anyone except Him, and [He has enjoined] kindness to parents. Should any of them or both reach old age at your side, do not say to them, ‘Fie!’ And do not chide them, but speak to them noble words.\nوَاخْفِضْ لَهُمَا جَنَاحَ الذُّلِّ مِنَ الرَّحْمَةِ وَقُلْ رَّبِّ ارْحَمْهُمَا كَمَا رَبَّيٰنِىْ صَغِيْرًا ؕ‏(24)\nWAKH FIZ LAHOMAA JANAAHAZ ZULLE MENAR RAHMATE WA QUR RABBIR HAMHOMAA KAMAA RABBAYAANEE SAGHEERAA.\nLower the wing of humility to them, mercifully, and say, ‘My Lord! Have mercy on them, just as they reared me when I was [a] small [child]!’\nرَّبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىْ نُفُوْسِكُمْؕ اِنْ تَكُوْنُوْا صٰلِحِيْنَ فَاِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِلْاَوَّابِيْنَ غَفُوْرًا‏(25)\nRABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAA FEE NOFOOSEKUM, IN TAKOONOO SAALEHEENA FA-INNAHU KAANA LIL-AWWAABEENA GHAFOORAA.\nYour Lord knows best what is in your hearts. Should you be righteous, He is indeed most forgiving toward penitents.\nوَاٰتِ ذَا الْقُرْبٰى حَقَّهٗ وَالْمِسْكِيْنَ وَابْنَ السَّبِيْلِ وَلَا تُبَذِّرْ تَبْذِيْرًا‏(26)\nWA AATE ZAL QURBAA HAQQAHU WAL MISKEENA WAB NAS SABEELE WA LAA TOBAZZIR TABZEERAA.\nGive the relatives their [due] right, and the needy and the traveller [as well], but do not squander wastefully.\nاِنَّ الْمُبَذِّرِيْنَ كَانُوْۤا اِخْوَانَ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ ؕ وَكَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لِرَبِّهٖ كَفُوْرًا‏(27)\nINNAL MOBAZZEREENA KAANOO IKHWAANASH SHAYAATEEN, WA KAANASH SHAYTAANO LE-RABBEHI KAFOORAA.\nIndeed the wasteful are brothers of satans, and Satan is ungrateful to his Lord.\nوَاِمَّا تُعْرِضَنَّ عَنْهُمُ ابْتِغَآءَ رَحْمَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ تَرْجُوْهَا فَقُلْ لَّهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّيْسُوْرًا‏(28)\nWA IMMAA TO’REZANNA A’NHOMUB TEGHAAA-A RAHMATIM MIR RABBEKA TARJOOHAA FA-QUL LAHUM QAWLAM MAYSOORAA.\nAnd if you have to hold off from [assisting] them [for now], seeking your Lord’s mercy which you expect [in the future], speak to them gentle words.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ يَدَكَ مَغْلُوْلَةً اِلٰى عُنُقِكَ وَلَا تَبْسُطْهَا كُلَّ الْبَسْطِ فَتَقْعُدَ مَلُوْمًا مَّحْسُوْرًا‏(29)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’L YADAKA MAGHLOOLATAN ELAA O’NOQEKA WA LAA TABSUTHAA KULLAL BASTE FA-TAQ-O’DA MALOOMAM MAHSOORAA.\nDo not keep your hand chained to your neck, nor open it altogether, or you will sit blameworthy and regretful.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(30)\nINNA RABBAKA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER, INNAHU KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERAM BASEERAA.\nIndeed your Lord expands the provision for whomever He wishes, and tightens it. Indeed, He is well aware of His servants and a keen observer.\nوَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَكُمْ خَشْيَةَ اِمْلَاقٍؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُهُمْ وَاِيَّاكُمْؕ اِنَّ قَتْلَهُمْ كَانَ خِطْاً كَبِيْرًا‏(31)\nWA LAA TAQTOLOO AWLAADAKUM KHASHYATA IMLAAQ, NAHNO NARZOQOHUM WA IYYAAKUM, INNA QATLAHUM KAANA KHIT-AN KABEERAA.\nDo not kill your children for the fear of penury: We will provide for them and for you. Killing them is indeed a great iniquity.\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الزِّنٰٓى اِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً  ؕ وَسَآءَ سَبِيْلًا‏(32)\nWA LAA TAQRABUZ ZENAA INNAHU KAANA FAAHESHAH, WA SAAA-A SABEELAA.\nDo not approach fornication. It is indeed an indecency and an evil way.\nوَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَمَنْ قُتِلَ مَظْلُوْمًا فَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا لِوَلِيِّهٖ سُلْطٰنًا فَلَا يُسْرِفْ فِّى الْقَتْلِ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مَنْصُوْرًا‏(33)\nWA LAA TAQTOLUN NAFSAL LATEE HARRAMAL LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQ, WA MAN QOTELA MAZLOOMAN FAQAD JA-A’LNAA LE-WALIYYEHI SULTAANAN FALAA YUSRIF FIL QATL, INNAHU KAANA MANSOORAA.\nDo not kill a soul [whose life] Allah has made inviolable, except with due cause, and whoever is killed wrongfully, We have certainly given his heir an authority. But let him not commit any excess in killing [the murderer], for he has been assisted [by law].\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوْا مَالَ الْيَتِيْمِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ اَشُدَّهٗ وَاَوْفُوْا بِالْعَهْدِۚ اِنَّ الْعَهْدَ كَانَ مَسْئُوْلًا‏(34)\nWA LAA TAQRABOO MAALAL YATEEME ILLAA BILLATEE HEYA AHSANO HATTAA YABLOGHA ASHUDDAH, WA AWFOO BIL-A’HD, INNAL A’HDA KAANA MAS-OOLAA.\nDo not approach the orphan’s property except in the best manner, until he comes of age. Fulfill the covenants; indeed all covenants are accountable.\nوَاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ اِذَا كِلْتُمْ وَزِنُوْا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيْمِؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَحْسَنُ تَاْوِيْلًا‏(35)\nWA AWFUL KAYLA EZAA KILTUM WA ZENOO BIL-QISTAASIL MUSTAQEEM, ZAALEKA KHAYRUNW WA AHSANO TAAWEELAA.\nWhen you measure, observe fully the measure, [and] weigh with an even balance. That is better and more favourable with respect to the outcome [in the Hereafter].\nوَلَا تَقْفُ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ؕ اِنَّ السَّمْعَ وَالْبَصَرَ وَالْفُؤَادَ كُلُّ اُولٰۤئِكَ كَانَ عَنْهُ مَسْئُوْلًا‏(36)\nWA LAA TAQFO MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LM, INNAS SAM-A’ WAL BASARA WAL FO-AADA KULLO OOLAAA-EKA KAANA A’NHO MAS-OOLAA.\nDo not pursue that of which you have no knowledge. Indeed hearing, eyesight, and the heart—all of these are accountable.\nوَلَا تَمْشِ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَحًا ۚ اِنَّكَ لَنْ تَخْرِقَ الْاَرْضَ وَلَنْ تَبْلُغَ الْجِبَالَ طُوْلًا‏(37)\nWA LAA TAMSHE FIL ARZE MARAHAA, INNAKA LAN TAKHREQAL ARZA WA LAN TABLOGHAL JEBAALA TOOLAA.\nDo not walk exultantly on the earth. Indeed, you will neither pierce the earth, nor reach the mountains in height.\nكُلُّ ذٰ لِكَ كَانَ سَيِّئُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ مَكْرُوْهًا‏(38)\nKULLO ZAALEKA KAANA SAYYE-OHU I’NDA RABBEKA MAKROOHAA.\nThe evil of all these is detestable to your Lord.\nذٰ لِكَ مِمَّاۤ اَوْحٰۤى اِلَيْكَ رَبُّكَ مِنَ الْحِكْمَةِ ؕ وَلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتُلْقٰى فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَلُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا‏(39)\nZAALEKA MIMMAA AWHAA ELAYKA RABBOKA MENAL HIKMAH, WA LAA TAJ-A’L MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA FA-TULQAA FEE JAHANNAMA MALOOMAM MADHOORAA.\nThese are among [precepts] that your Lord has revealed to you of wisdom. Do not set up another god besides Allah, or you will be cast into hell, being blameworthy and banished [from His mercy].\nاَفَاَصْفٰٮكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِالْبَنِيْنَ وَ اتَّخَذَ مِنَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنَاثًا ؕ اِنَّكُمْ لَتَقُوْلُوْنَ قَوْلًا عَظِيْمًا‏(40)\nAFA-ASFAAKUM RABBOKUM BIL-BANEENA WAT TAKHAZA MENAL MALAAA-EKATE ENAASAA, INNAKUM LATAQOOLOONA QAWLAN A’ZEEMAA.\nDid your Lord prefer you for sons, and [Himself] adopt females from among the angels? Indeed, you say a monstrous word!\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لِيَذَّكَّرُوْا ؕ وَمَا يَزِيْدُهُمْ اِلَّا نُفُوْرًا‏(41)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA FEE HAAZAL QUR-AANE LE-YAZZAKKAROO, WA MAA YAZEEDOHUM ILLAA NOFOORAA.\nCertainly We have variously paraphrased [the principles of guidance] in this Quran so that they may take admonition, but it increases them only in aversion.\nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ مَعَهٗۤ اٰلِهَةٌ كَمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِذًا لَّابْتَغَوْا اِلٰى ذِى الْعَرْشِ سَبِيْلًا‏(42)\nQUL LAW KAANA MA-A’HU AALEHATUN KAMAA YAQOOLOONA EZAL LABTAGHAW ELAA ZIL A’RSHE SABEELAA.\nSay, ‘Were there [other] gods besides Him, as they say, they would surely have encroached on the Lord of the Throne.\nسُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يَقُوْلُوْنَ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(43)\nSUBHAANAHU WA TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YAQOOLOONA O’LUWWAN KABEERAA.\nImmaculate is He, and greatly exalted above what they say!’\nتُسَبِّحُ لَهُ السَّمٰوٰتُ السَّبْعُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّؕ وَاِنْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تَفْقَهُوْنَ تَسْبِيْحَهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حَلِيْمًا غَفُوْرًا‏(44)\nTOSABBEHO LAHUS SAMAAWAATUS SAB-O’ WAL ARZO WA MAN FEEHIN, WA IM MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA YOSABBEHO BE-HAMDEHI WA LAAKIL LAA TAFQAHOONA TASBEEHAHUM, INNAHU KAANA HALEEMAN GHAFOORAA.\nThe seven heavens glorify Him, and the earth [too], and whoever is in them. There is not a thing but celebrates His praise, but you do not understand their glorification. Indeed, He is all-forbearing, all-forgiving.\nوَاِذَا قَرَاْتَ الْقُرْاٰنَ جَعَلْنَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ حِجَابًا مَّسْتُوْرًا ۙ‏(45)\nWA EZAA QARAA-TAL QUR-AANA JA-A’LNAA BAYNAKA WA BAYNAL LAZEENA LAA YOA-MINOONA BIL AAKHERATE HEJAABAM MASTOORAA.\nWhen you recite the Quran, We draw a hidden curtain between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter,\nوَّجَعَلْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اَكِنَّةً اَنْ يَّفْقَهُوْهُ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًا ؕ وَاِذَا ذَكَرْتَ رَبَّكَ فِى الْقُرْاٰنِ وَحْدَهٗ وَلَّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهِمْ نُفُوْرًا‏(46)\nWA JA-A’LNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM AKINNATAN ANY YAFQAHOOHO WA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRAA, WA EZAA ZAKARTA RABBAKA FIL QUR-AANE WAHDAHU WALLAW A’LAA ADBAAREHIM NOFOORAA.\nand We cast veils on their hearts, lest they should understand it, and a deafness into their ears. When you mention your Lord alone in the Quran, they turn their backs in aversion.\nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ بِهٖۤ اِذْ يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ وَاِذْ هُمْ نَجْوٰٓى اِذْ يَقُوْلُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا رَجُلًا مَّسْحُوْرًا‏(47)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YASTAME-O’ONA BEHI IZ YASTAME-O’ONA ELAYKA WA IZ HUM NAJWAA IZ YAQOOLUZ ZAALEMOONA IN TATTABE-O’ONA ILLAA RAJOLAM MASHOORAA.\nWe know best what they listen for, when they listen to you, and when they hold their secret talks, when the wrongdoers say, ‘[If you follow him] You will be following just a bewitched man.’\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ ضَرَبُوْا لَكَ الْاَمْثَالَ فَضَلُّوْا فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَبِيْلًا‏(48)\nUNZUR KAYFA ZARABOO LAKAL AMSAALA FA-ZALLOO FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SABEELAA.\nLook, how they coin epithets for you; so they go astray, and cannot find a way.\nوَقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا وَّرُفَاتًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ خَلْقًا جَدِيْدًا‏(49)\nWA QAALOO A-EZAA KUNNAA E’ZAAMANW WA ROFAATAN A-INNAA LA-MAB-O’OSOONA KHALQAN JADEEDAA.\nThey say, ‘What, when we have become bones and dust, shall we really be raised in a new creation?’\nقُلْ كُوْنُوْا حِجَارَةً اَوْ حَدِيْدًا‏(50)\nQUL KOONOO HEJAARATAN AW HADEEDAA.\nSay, ‘[That is bound to happen] even if you should become stones, or iron,\nاَوْ خَلْقًا مِّمَّا يَكْبُرُ فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْۚ فَسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَنْ يُّعِيْدُنَا ؕ قُلِ الَّذِىْ فَطَرَكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ۚ فَسَيُنْغِضُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ رُءُوْسَهُمْ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هُوَ ؕ قُلْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ قَرِيْبًا‏(51)\nAW KHALQAM MIMMAA YAKBORO FEE SODOOREKUM, FASAYAQOOLOONA MAN-Y YO-E’EDONAA, QOLIL LAZEE FATARAKUM AWWALA MARRAH, FASAYUNGHEZOONA ELAYKA RO-OOSAHUM WA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HOO, QUL A’SAA AN-Y YAKOONA QAREEBAA.\nor a creature more fantastic to your minds!’ They will say, ‘Who will bring us back?’ Say, ‘He who originated you the first time.’ They will nod their heads at you, and say, ‘When will that be?’ Say, ‘Maybe it is near!\nيَوْمَ يَدْعُوْكُمْ فَتَسْتَجِيْبُوْنَ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَتَظُنُّوْنَ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(52)\nYAWMA YAD-O’OKUM FA-TASTAJEEBOONA BE-HAMDEHI WA TAZUNNOONA IL LABISTUM ILLAA QALEELAA.\nThe day He calls you, you will respond to Him, praising Him, and you will think you remained [in the world] only for a little while.’\nوَقُلْ لِّعِبَادِىْ يَقُوْلُوا الَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ يَنْزَغُ بَيْنَهُمْؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ كَانَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ عَدُوًّا مُّبِيْنًا‏(53)\nWA QUL LE-E’BAADEE YAQOOLUL LATEE HEYA AHSAN, INNASH SHAYTAANA YANZAGHO BAYNAHUM, INNASH SHAYTAANA KAANA LIL-INSAANE A’DUWWAM MOBEENAA.\nTell My servants to speak in a manner which is the best. Indeed Satan incites ill feeling between them, and Satan is indeed man’s manifest enemy.\nرَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يَرْحَمْكُمْ اَوْ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُعَذِّبْكُمْ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيْلًا‏(54)\nRABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEKUM, IN-Y YASHAA YARHAMKUM AW IN-Y YASHAA YO-A’ZZIBKUM, WA MAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM WAKEELAA.\nYour Lord knows you best. He will have mercy on you if He wishes, or punish you, if He wishes, and We did not send you to watch over them.\nوَرَبُّكَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَلَقَدْ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَ النَّبِيّٖنَ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّاٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ زَبُوْرًا‏(55)\nWA RABBOKA A-A’LAMO BEMAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WA LAQAD FAZZALNAA BA’ZAN NABIYYEENA A’LAA BA’ZINW WA AATAYNAA DAAWOODA ZABOORAA.\nYour Lord knows best whoever is in the heavens and the earth. Certainly, We gave some prophets an advantage over the others, and We gave David the Psalms.\nقُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ كَشْفَ الضُّرِّ عَنْكُمْ وَلَا تَحْوِيْلًا‏(56)\nQOLID U’L LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM MIN DOONEHI FALAA YAMLEKOONA KASHFAZ ZURRE A’NKUM WA LAA TAHWEELAA.\nSay, ‘Invoke those whom you claim [to be gods] besides Him. They have no power to remove your distress, nor to bring about any change [in your state].\nاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ يَبْتَغُوْنَ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمُ الْوَسِيْلَةَ اَيُّهُمْ اَقْرَبُ وَيَرْجُوْنَ رَحْمَتَهٗ وَيَخَافُوْنَ عَذَابَهٗؕ اِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ كَانَ مَحْذُوْرًا‏(57)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA YABTAGHOONA ELAA RABBEHEMUL WASEELATA AYYOHUM AQRABO WA YARJOONA RAHMATAHU WA YAKHAAFOONA A’ZAABAH, INNA A’ZAABA RABBEKA KAANA MAHZOORAA.\nThey [themselves] are the ones who supplicate, seeking a recourse to their Lord, whoever is nearer [to Him], expecting His mercy and fearing His punishment.’ Indeed your Lord’s punishment is a thing to beware of.\nوَاِنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا نَحْنُ مُهْلِكُوْهَا قَبْلَ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَوْ مُعَذِّبُوْهَا عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ كَانَ ذٰ لِكَ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مَسْطُوْرًا‏(58)\nWA IM MIN QARYATIN ILLAA NAHNO MOHLEKOOHAA QABLA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE AW MO-A’ZZEBOOHAA A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA, KAANA ZAALEKA FIL KETAABE MASTOORAA.\nThere is not a town but We will destroy it before the Day of Resurrection, or punish it with a severe punishment. That has been written in the Book.\nوَمَا مَنَعَنَاۤ اَنْ نُّرْسِلَ بِالْاٰيٰتِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ كَذَّبَ بِهَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ وَاٰتَيْنَا ثَمُوْدَ النَّاقَةَ مُبْصِرَةً فَظَلَمُوْا بِهَاؕ وَمَا نُرْسِلُ بِالْاٰيٰتِ اِلَّا تَخْوِيْفًا‏(59)\nWA MAA MANA-A’NAA AN NURSELA BIL-AAYAATE ILLAA AN KAZZABA BEHAL AWWALOON, WA AATAYNAA SAMOODAN NAAQATA MUBSERATAN FA-ZALAMOO BEHAA, WA MAA NURSELO BIL-AAYAATE ILLAA TAKHWEEFAA.\nNothing keeps Us from sending signs except that the former peoples denied them. We gave Thamud the she-camel as an eye-opener, but they wronged her. We do not send the signs except as warning.\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لَكَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ اَحَاطَ بِالنَّاسِ ؕ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الرُّءْيَا الَّتِىْۤ اَرَيْنٰكَ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَ الشَّجَرَةَ الْمَلْعُوْنَةَ فِى الْقُرْاٰنِ ؕ وَنُخَوِّفُهُمْۙ فَمَا يَزِيْدُهُمْ اِلَّا طُغْيَانًا كَبِيْرًا‏(60)\nWA IZ QULNAA LAKA INNA RABBAKA AHAATA BIN-NAAS, WA MAA JA-A’LNAR ROAYAL LATEE ARAYNAAKA ILLAA FITNATAL LIN-NAASE WASH SHAJARATAL MAL-O’ONATA FIL QUR-AAN, WA NOKHAWWEFOHUM, FAMAA YAZEEDOHUM ILLAA TUGHYAANAN KABEERAA.\nWhen We said to you, ‘Indeed your Lord encircles those people,’ We did not appoint the vision that We showed you except as a tribulation for the people and the tree cursed in the Quran. We warn them, but it only increases them in their outrageous rebellion.\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَ قَالَ ءَاَسْجُدُ لِمَنْ خَلَقْتَ طِيْنًا ۚ‏(61)\nWA IZ QULNAA LIL-MALAAA-EKATIS JODOO LE-AADAMA FA-SAJADOO ILLAA IBLEESA QAALA A-ASJODO LEMAN KHALAQTA TEENAA.\nWhen We said to the angels, ‘Prostrate before Adam,’ they [all] prostrated, but not Iblis: he said, ‘Shall I prostrate before someone whom You have created from clay?’\nقَالَ اَرَءَيْتَكَ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كَرَّمْتَ عَلَىَّ لَئِنْ اَخَّرْتَنِ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَاَحْتَنِكَنَّ ذُرِّيَّتَهٗۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(62)\nQAALA ARA-AYTAKA HAAZAL LAZEE KARRAMTA A’LAYY, LA-IN AKH-KHARTANE ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LA-AHTANEKANNA ZURRIYYATAHU ILLAA QALEELAA.\nSaid he, ‘Do You see this one whom You have honoured above me? If You respite me until the Day of Resurrection, I will surely lay my yoke on his progeny, [all] except a few.’\nقَالَ اذْهَبْ فَمَنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ فَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ جَزَآؤُكُمْ جَزَآءً مَّوْفُوْرًا‏(63)\nQAALAZ HAB FAMAN TABE-A’KA MINHUM FA-INNA JAHANNAMA JAZAAA-OKUM JAZAAA-AM MAWFOORAA.\nSaid He, ‘Begone! Whoever of them follows you, indeed the hell shall be your requital, an ample reward.\nوَاسْتَفْزِزْ مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ مِنْهُمْ بِصَوْتِكَ وَاَجْلِبْ عَلَيْهِمْ بِخَيْلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَ وَشَارِكْهُمْ فِى الْاَمْوَالِ وَالْاَوْلَادِ وَعِدْهُمْ ؕ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا‏(64)\nWAS TAFZIZ MANIS TATA’TA MINHUM BE-SAWTEKA WA AJLIB A’LAYHIM BE-KHAYLEKA WA RAJELEKA WA SHAARIKHUM FIL AMWAALE WAL AWLAADE WA I’DHUM, WA MAA YA-E’DOHOMUSH SHAYTAANO ILLAA GHOROORAA.\nInstigate whomever of them you can with your voice; and rally against them your cavalry and your infantry, and share with them in wealth and children, and make promises to them!’ But Satan promises them nothing but delusion.\nاِنَّ عِبَادِىْ لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنٌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ وَكِيْلًا‏(65)\nINNA E’BAADEE LAYSA LAKA A’LAYHIM SULTAAN, WA KAFAA BE-RABBEKA WAKEELAA.\n‘As for My servants, you shall have no authority over them.’ And your Lord suffices as trustee.\nرَبُّكُمُ الَّذِىْ يُزْجِىْ لَكُمُ الْفُلْكَ فِى الْبَحْرِ لِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيْمًا‏(66)\nRABBOKOMUL LAZEE YUZJEE LAKOMUL FULKA FIL BAHRE LE-TABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEH, INNAHU KAANA BEKUM RAHEEMAA.\nYour Lord is He who drives for you the ships in the sea that you may seek of His bounty. Indeed, He is most merciful to you.\nوَاِذَا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فِى الْبَحْرِ ضَلَّ مَنْ تَدْعُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا نَجّٰٮكُمْ اِلَى الْبَرِّ اَعْرَضْتُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ كَفُوْرًا‏(67)\nWA EZAA MASSAKOMUZ ZURRO FIL BAHRE ZALLA MAN TAD-O’ONA ILLAA IYYAAH, FALAMMAA NAJJAAKUM ELAL BARRE A-A’RAZTUM, WA KAANAL INSAANO KAFOORAA.\nWhen distress befalls you at sea, those whom you invoke besides Him are forsaken. But when He delivers you to land, you are disregardful [of Him]. Man is very ungrateful.\nاَفَاَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ يَّخْسِفَ بِكُمْ جَانِبَ الْبَرِّ اَوْ يُرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ حَاصِبًا ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْالَكُمْ وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(68)\nAFA-AMINTUM AN-Y YAKHSEFA BEKUM JAANEBAL BARRE AW YURSELA A’LAYKUM HAASEBAN SUMMA LAA TAJEDOO LAKUM WAKEELAA.\nDo you feel secure that He will not make the coastland swallow you, or He will not unleash upon you a rain of stones? Then you will not find any defender for yourselves.\nاَمْ اَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ يُّعِيْدَكُمْ فِيْهِ تَارَةً اُخْرٰى فَيُرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ قَاصِفًا مِّنَ الرِّيْحِ فَيُغْرِقَكُمْ بِمَا كَفَرْتُمْۙ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْا لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا بِهٖ تَبِيْعًا‏(69)\nAM AMINTUM AN-Y YO-E’EDAKUM FEEHE TAARATAN UKHRAA FA-YURSELA A’LAYKUM QAASEFAM MENAR REEHE FA-YUGHREQAKUM BEMAA KAFARTUM, SUMMA LAA TAJEDOO LAKUM A’LAYNAA BEHI TABEE-A’A.\nDo you feel secure that He will not send you back into it another time and unleash against you a shattering gale and drown you because of your unfaith? Then you will not find for yourselves any redresser against Us.\nوَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ وَحَمَلْنٰهُمْ فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلٰى كَثِيْرٍ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقْنَا تَفْضِيْلًا‏(70)\nWA LAQAD KARRAMNAA BANEE AADAMA WA HAMALNAAHUM FIL BARRE WAL BAHRE WA RAZAQNAAHUM MENAT TAYYEBAATE WA FAZZALNAAHUM A’LAA KASEERIM MIMMAN KHALAQNAA TAFZEELAA.\nCertainly We have honoured the Children of Adam, and carried them over land and sea, and provided them with all the good things, and preferred them with a complete preference over many of those We have created.\nيَوْمَ نَدْعُوْا كُلَّ اُنَاسٍۢ بِاِمَامِهِمْۚ فَمَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِيَمِيْنِهٖ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ يَقْرَءُوْنَ كِتٰبَهُمْ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(71)\nYAWMA NAD-O’O KULLA ONAASIM BE-EMAAMEHIM, FAMAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BE-YAMEENEHI FA-OOLAAA-EKA YAQRA-OONA KETAABAHUM WA LAA YUZLAMOONA FATEELAA.\nThe day We shall summon every group of people along with their imam, then whoever is given his book in his right hand—they will read it, and they will not be wronged so much as a single date-thread.\nوَمَنْ كَانَ فِىْ هٰذِهٖۤ اَعْمٰى فَهُوَ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اَعْمٰى وَاَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(72)\nWA MAN KAANA FEE HAAZEHI A-A’MAA FAHOWA FIL AAKHERATE A-A’MAA WA AZALLO SABEELAA.\nBut whoever has been blind in this [world], will be blind in the Hereafter, and [even] more astray from the [right] way.\nوَاِنْ كَادُوْا لَيَفْتِنُوْنَكَ عَنِ الَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ لِتَفْتَرِىَ عَلَيْنَا غَيْرَهٗ ۖ  وَاِذًا لَّاتَّخَذُوْكَ خَلِيْلًا‏(73)\nWA IN KAADOO LAYAFTENOONAKA A’NIL LAZEE AWHAYNAA ELAYKA LE-TAFTAREYA A’LAYNAA GHAYRAH, WA EZAL LATTAKHAZOOKA KHALEELAA.\nThey were about to beguile you from what Allah has revealed to you so that you may fabricate something other than that against Us, whereat they would have befriended you.\nوَلَوْلَاۤ اَنْ ثَبَّتْنٰكَ لَقَدْ كِدْتَّ تَرْكَنُ اِلَيْهِمْ شَيْئًا قَلِيْلًا  ۙ‏(74)\nWA LAWLAA AN SABBATNAAKA LAQAD KITTA TARKANO ELAYHIM SHAY-AN QALEELAA.\nAnd had We not fortified you, certainly you might have inclined toward them a bit.\nاِذًا لَّاَذَقْنٰكَ ضِعْفَ الْحَيٰوةِ وَضِعْفَ الْمَمَاتِ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ عَلَيْنَا نَصِيْرًا‏(75)\nEZAL LA-AZAQNAAKA ZE’FAL HAYAATE WA ZE’FAL MAMAATE SUMMA LAA TAJEDO LAKA A’LAYNAA NASEERAA.\nThen We would have surely made you taste a double [punishment] in this life and a double [punishment] after death, and then you would have not found for yourself any helper against Us.\nوَاِنْ كَادُوْا لَيَسْتَفِزُّوْنَكَ مِنَ الْاَرْضِ لِيُخْرِجُوْكَ مِنْهَا وَاِذًا لَّا يَلْبَثُوْنَ خِلٰفَكَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(76)\nWA IN KAADOO LAYASTAFIZZOONAKA MENAL ARZE LE-YUKHREJOOKA MINHAA WA EZAL LAA YALBASOONA KHELAAFAKA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nThey were about to hound you out of the land, to expel you from it, but then they would not have stayed after you but a little.\nسُنَّةَ مَنْ قَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنْ رُّسُلِنَا وَلَا تَجِدُ لِسُنَّتِنَا تَحْوِيْلًا‏(77)\nSUNNATA MAN QAD ARSALNAA QABLAKA MIR ROSOLENAA WA LAA TAJEDO LE-SUNNATENAA TAHWEELAA.\nA precedent concerning those We have sent before you from among Our apostles, and you will not find any change in Our precedent.\nاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِدُلُوْكِ الشَّمْسِ اِلٰى غَسَقِ الَّيْلِ وَقُرْاٰنَ الْفَجْرِؕ اِنَّ قُرْاٰنَ الْفَجْرِ كَانَ مَشْهُوْدًا‏(78)\nAQEMIS SALAATA LE-DOLOOKISH SHAMSE ELAA GHASAQIL LAYLE WA QUR-AANAL FAJR, INNA QUR-AANAL FAJRE KAANA MASH-HOODAA.\nMaintain the prayer [during the period] from the sun’s decline till the darkness of the night, and [observe particularly] the dawn recital. Indeed the dawn recital is attended [by angels].\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَتَهَجَّدْ بِهٖ نَافِلَةً لَّكَ ۖ  عَسٰۤى اَنْ يَّبْعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامًا مَّحْمُوْدًا‏(79)\nWA MENAL LAYLE FA-TAHAJJAD BEHI NAAFELATAL LAK, A’SAA AN-Y YAB-A’SAKA RABBOKA MAQAAMAM MAHMOODAA.\nAnd keep vigil for a part of the night, as a supererogatory [devotion] for you. It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station.\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَدْخِلْنِىْ مُدْخَلَ صِدْقٍ وَّ اَخْرِجْنِىْ مُخْرَجَ صِدْقٍ وَّاجْعَلْ لِّىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ سُلْطٰنًا نَّصِيْرًا‏(80)\nWA QUR RABBE ADKHILNEE MUDKHALA SIDQINW WA AKHRIJNEE MUKHRAJA SIDQINW WAJ A’L LEE MIL LADUNKA SULTAANAN NASEERAA.\nAnd say, ‘My Lord! ‘Admit me with a worthy entrance, and bring me out with a worthy departure, and render me a favourable authority from Yourself.’\nوَقُلْ جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ الْبَاطِلُؕ اِنَّ الْبَاطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوْقًا‏(81)\nWA QUL JAAA-AL HAQQO WA ZAHAQAL BAATEL, INNAL BAATELA KAANA ZAHOOQAA.\nAnd say, ‘The truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is bound to vanish.’\nوَنُنَزِّلُ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِ مَا هُوَ شِفَآءٌ وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ وَلَا يَزِيْدُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ اِلَّا خَسَارًا‏(82)\nWA NONAZZELO MENAL QUR-AANE MAA HOWA SHEFAAA-UNW WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEENA, WA LAA YAZEEDUZ ZAALEMEENA ILLAA KHASAARAA.\nWe send down in the Quran that which is a cure and mercy for the faithful; and it increases the wrongdoers only in loss.\nوَاِذَاۤ اَنْعَمْنَا عَلَى الْاِنْسَانِ اَعْرَضَ وَنَاٰ بِجَانِبِهٖۚ وَاِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ كَانَ يَئُوْسًا‏(83)\nWA EZAA AN-A’MNAA A’LAL INSAANE A-A’RAZA WA NA-AA BE-JAANEBEH, WA EZAA MASSAHUSH SHARRO KAANA YA-OOSAA.\nWhen We bless man, he is disregardful and turns aside; but when an ill befalls him, he is despondent.\nقُلْ كُلٌّ يَّعْمَلُ عَلٰى شَاكِلَتِهٖؕ فَرَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ هُوَ اَهْدٰى سَبِيْلًا‏(84)\nQUL KULLUN-Y YA’MALO A’LAA SHAAKELATEH, FA-RABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAN HOWA AHDAA SABEELAA.\nSay, ‘Everyone acts according to his character. Your Lord knows best who is better guided with regard to the way.’\nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الرُّوْحِ ؕ قُلِ الرُّوْحُ مِنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّىْ وَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(85)\nWA YAS-ALOONAKA A’NIR ROOH, QOLIR ROOHO MIN AMRE RABBEE WA MAA OOTEETUM MENAL I’LME ILLAA QALEELAA.\nThey question you concerning the Spirit. Say, ‘The Spirit is of the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of the knowledge except a few [of you].’\nوَلَئِنْ شِئْنَا لَنَذْهَبَنَّ بِالَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ بِهٖ عَلَيْنَا وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(86)\nWA LA-IN SHEANAA LANAZHABANNA BILLAZEE AWHAYNAA ELAYKA SUMMA LAA TAJEDO LAKA BEHI A’LAYNAA WAKEELAA.\nIf We wish, We would take away what We have revealed to you. Then you would not find for yourself any defender against Us,\nاِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ ؕ اِنَّ فَضْلَهٗ كَانَ عَلَيْكَ كَبِيْرًا‏(87)\nILLAA RAHMATAM MIR RABBEK, INNA FAZLAHU KAANA A’LAYKA KABEERAA.\nexcept a mercy from your Lord. Indeed His grace has been great upon you.\nقُلْ لَّئِنِ اجْتَمَعَتِ الْاِنْسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتُوْا بِمِثْلِ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لَا يَاْتُوْنَ بِمِثْلِهٖ وَلَوْ كَانَ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ ظَهِيْرًا‏(88)\nQUL LA-ENIJ TAMA-A’TIL INSO WAL JINNO A’LAA AN-Y YAATOO BE-MISLE HAAZAL QUR-AANE LAA YAATOONA BE-MISLEHI WA LAW KAANA BA’ZOHUM LE-BA’ZIN ZAHEERAA.\nSay, ‘Should all humans and jinn rally to bring the like of this Quran, they will not bring its like, even if they assisted one another.’\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ كُلِّ مَثَلٍ فَاَبٰٓى اَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(89)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA LIN-NAASE FEE HAAZAL QUR-AANE MIN KULLE MASAL, FA-ABAA AKSARUN NAASE ILLAA KOFOORAA.\nWe have certainly interspersed this Quran with every [kind of] parable for the people, but most people are only intent on ingratitude.\nوَقَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتّٰى تَفْجُرَ لَنَا مِنَ الْاَرْضِ يَنْۢبُوْعًا ۙ‏(90)\nWA QAALOO LAN NOAMENA LAKA HATTAA TAFJORA LANAA MENAL ARZE YAMBOO-A’A.\nThey say, ‘We will not believe you until you make a spring gush forth for us from the ground.\nاَوْ تَكُوْنَ لَكَ جَنَّةٌ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّعِنَبٍ فَتُفَجِّرَ الْاَنْهٰرَ خِلٰلَهَا تَفْجِيْرًا ۙ‏(91)\nAW TAKOONA LAKA JANNATUM MIN NAKHEELINW WA E’NABIN FA-TOFAJJERAL ANHAARA KHELAALAHAA TAFJEERAA.\nOr until you have a garden of date palms and vines and you make streams gush through it.\nاَوْ تُسْقِطَ السَّمَآءَ كَمَا زَعَمْتَ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا اَوْ تَاْتِىَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ قَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(92)\nAW TUSQETAS SAMAAA-A KAMAA ZA-A’MTA A’LAYNAA KESAFAN AW TAATEYA BIL-LAAHE WAL MALAAA-EKATE QABEELAA.\nOr until you cause the sky to fall in fragments upon us, just as you have averred. Or until you bring Allah and the angels [right] in front of us.\nاَوْ يَكُوْنَ لَكَ بَيْتٌ مِّنْ زُخْرُفٍ اَوْ تَرْقٰى فِى السَّمَآءِ ؕ وَلَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لِرُقِيِّكَ حَتّٰى تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا كِتٰبًا نَّقْرَؤُهٗ ؕ قُلْ سُبْحَانَ رَبِّىْ هَلْ كُنْتُ اِلَّا بَشَرًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(93)\nAW YAKOONA LAKA BAYTUM MIN ZUKHROFIN AW TARQAA FIS SAMAAA, WA LAN NOAMENA LE-ROQIYYEKA HATTAA TONAZZELA A’LAYNAA KETAABAN NAQRA-OH, QUL SUBHAANA RABBEE HAL KUNTO ILLAA BASHARAR RASOOLAA.\nOr until you have a house of gold, or you ascend into the sky. And we will not believe your ascension until you bring down for us a book that we may read.’ Say, ‘Immaculate is my Lord! Am I anything but a human apostle?!’\nوَمَا مَنَعَ النَّاسَ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْۤا اِذْ جَآءَهُمُ الْهُدٰٓى اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَبَعَثَ اللّٰهُ بَشَرًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(94)\nWA MAA MANA-A’N NAASA AN-Y YOAMENOO IZ JAAA-AHOMUL HODAA ILLAA AN QAALOO ABA-A’SAL LAAHO BASHARAR RASOOLAA.\nNothing has kept these people from believing when guidance came to them, but their saying, ‘Has Allah sent a human as an apostle?!’\nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَلٰۤئِكَةٌ يَّمْشُوْنَ مُطْمَئِنِّيْنَ لَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَلَكًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(95)\nQUL LAW KAANA FIL ARZE MALAAA-EKATUN-Y YAMSHOONA MUTMA-INNEENA LANAZZALNAA A’LAYHIM MENAS SAMAAA-E MALAKAR RASOOLAA.\nSay, ‘Had there been angels in the earth, walking around and residing [in it like humans do], We would have sent down to them an angel from the heaven as apostle.’\nقُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(96)\nQUL KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAM BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM, INNAHU KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERAM BASEERAA.\nSay, ‘Allah suffices as witness between me and you. Indeed He is well aware His servants and a keen observer.’\nوَمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلْ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ ؕ وَنَحْشُرُهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْ عُمْيًا وَّبُكْمًا وَّصُمًّا ؕ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ ؕ كُلَّمَا خَبَتْ زِدْنٰهُمْ سَعِيْرًا‏(97)\nWA MAN-Y YAHDIL LAAHO FAHOWAL MOHTAD, WA MAN-Y YUZLIL FALAN TAJEDA LAHUM AWLEYAAA-A MIN DOONEH, WA NAHSHOROHUM YAWMAL QEYAAMATE A’LAA WOJOOHEHIM U’MYANW WA BUKMANW WA SUMMAA, MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM, KULLAMAA KHABAT ZIDNAAHUM SA-E’ERAA.\nWhomever Allah guides is rightly guided, and whomever He leads astray—you will never for find them any guardians besides Him. On the Day of Resurrection, We shall muster them [scrambling] on their faces, blind, dumb, and deaf. Their refuge shall be hell. Whenever it subsides, We shall intensify the blaze for them.\nذٰلِكَ جَزَآؤُهُمْ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا وَّرُفَاتًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ خَلْقًا جَدِيْدًا‏(98)\nZAALEKA JAZAAA-OHUM BE-ANNAHUM KAFAROO BE-AAYAATENAA WA QAALOO A-EZAA KUNNAA E’ZAAMANW WA ROFAATAN A-INNAA LA-MAB-O’OSOONA KHALQAN JADEEDAA.\nThat is their requital because they defied Our signs and said, ‘What, when we have become bones and dust, shall we really be raised in a new creation?’\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ قَادِرٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّخْلُقَ مِثْلَهُمْ وَجَعَلَ لَهُمْ اَجَلًا لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ ؕ فَاَبَى الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(99)\nAWA LAM YARAW ANNAL LAAHAL LAZEE KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA QAADERUN A’LAA AN-Y YAKHLOQA MISLAHUM WA JA-A’LA LAHUM AJALAL LAA RAYBA FEEH, FA-ABAZ ZAALEMOONA ILLAA KOFOORAA.\nDo they not see that Allah, who created the heavens and the earth, is able to create the like of them? He has appointed for them a term, in which there is no doubt; yet the wrongdoers are only intent on ingratitude.\nقُلْ لَّوْ اَنْتُمْ تَمْلِكُوْنَ خَزَآئِنَ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّاَمْسَكْتُمْ خَشْيَةَ الْاِنْفَاقِ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ قَتُوْرًا‏(100)\nQUL LAW ANTUM TAMLEKOONA KHAZAAA-ENA RAHMATE RABBEE EZAL LA-AMSAKTUM KHASHYATAL INFAAQ, WA KAANAL INSAANO QATOORAA.\nSay, ‘Even if you possessed the treasuries of my Lord’s mercy, you would withhold them for the fear of being spent, and man is very niggardly.’\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى تِسْعَ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍ فَسْئَلْ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ فَقَالَ لَهٗ فِرْعَوْنُ اِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّكَ يٰمُوْسٰى مَسْحُوْرًا‏(101)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAA TIS-A’ AAYAATIM BAYYENAATIN FAS-AL BANEE ISRAAA-EELA IZ JAAA-AHUM FA-QAALA LAHU FIR-A’WNO INNEE LA-AZUNNOKA YAA MOOSAA MASHOORAA.\nCertainly We gave Moses nine manifest signs. So ask the Children of Israel. When he came to them, Pharaoh said to him, ‘O Moses, indeed I think you are bewitched.’\nقَالَ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اِلَّا رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ بَصَآئِرَ ۚ وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّكَ يٰفِرْعَوْنُ مَثْبُوْرًا‏(102)\nQAALA LAQAD A’LIMTA MAA ANZALA HAA-OLAAA-E ILLAA RABBUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE BASAAA-ER, WA INNEE LA-AZUNNOKA YAA FIR-A’WNO MASBOORAA.\nHe said, ‘You certainly know that no one has sent these [signs] except the Lord of the heavens and the earth, as eye-openers, and I, O Pharaoh, indeed think you are doomed.’\nفَاَرَادَ اَنْ يَّسْتَفِزَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُ وَ مَنْ مَّعَهٗ جَمِيْعًا ۙ‏(103)\nFA-ARAADA AN-Y YASTAFIZZAHUM MENAL ARZE FA-AGHRAQNAAHO WA MAM MA-A’HU JAMEE-A’A.\nHe desired to exterminate them from the land, so We drowned him and all those who were with him.\nوَّقُلْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ لِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ اسْكُنُوا الْاَرْضَ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ الْاٰخِرَةِ جِئْنَا بِكُمْ لَفِيْفًا ؕ‏(104)\nWA QULNAA MIM BA’DEHI LE-BANEE ISRAAA-EELAS KONUL ARZA FA-EZAA JAAA-A WA’DUL AAKHERATE JEANAA BEKUM LAFEEFAA.\nAfter him We said to the Children of Israel, ‘Take up residence in the land, and when the occasion of the other [promise] comes, We shall gather you in mixed company.’\nوَبِالْحَقِّ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ وَبِالْحَقِّ نَزَلَ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا ۘ‏(105)\nWA BIL-HAQQE ANZALNAAHO WA BIL-HAQQE NAZAL, WA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA MOBASH-SHERANW WA NAZEERAA.\nWith the truth did We send it down, and with the truth did it descend, and We did not send you except as a bearer of good news and as a warner.\nوَقُرْاٰنًا فَرَقْنٰهُ لِتَقْرَاَهٗ عَلَى النَّاسِ عَلٰى مُكْثٍ وَّنَزَّلْنٰهُ تَنْزِيْلًا‏(106)\nWA QUR-AANAN FARAQNAAHO LE-TAQRA-AHU A’LAN NAASE A’LAA MUKSINW WA NAZZALNAAHO TANZEELAA.\nWe have sent the Quran in [discrete] parts so that you may recite it for the people a little at a time, and We have sent it down piecemeal.\nقُلْ اٰمِنُوْا بِهٖۤ اَوْ لَا تُؤْمِنُوْٓا ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖۤ اِذَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ يَخِرُّوْنَ لِلْاَذْقَانِ سُجَّدًا ۙ‏(107)\nQUL AAMENOO BEHI AW LAA TOAMENOO, INNAL LAZEENA OOTUL I’LMA MIN QABLEHI EZAA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM YAKHIRROONA LIL-AZQAANE SUJJADAA.\nSay, ‘Whether you believe in it, or do not believe in it, indeed when it is recited to those who were given knowledge before it, they fall down in prostration on their faces,\nوَّيَقُوْلُوْنَ سُبْحٰنَ رَبِّنَاۤ اِنْ كَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّنَا لَمَفْعُوْلًا‏(108)\nWA YAQOOLOONA SUBHAANA RABBENAA IN KAANA WA’DO RABBENAA LA-MAF-O’OLAA.\nand say, ‘‘Immaculate is our Lord! Indeed Our Lord’s promise is bound to be fulfilled.’’\nوَيَخِرُّوْنَ لِلْاَذْقَانِ يَبْكُوْنَ وَيَزِيْدُهُمْ خُشُوْعًا ۩‏(109)\nWA YAKHIRROONA LIL-AZQAANE YABKOONA WA YAZEEDOHUM KHOSHOO-A’A.\nWeeping, they fall down on their faces, and it increases them in humility.’\nقُلِ ادْعُوا اللّٰهَ اَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمٰنَ ؕ اَ يًّا مَّا تَدْعُوْا فَلَهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى ۚ وَلَا تَجْهَرْ بِصَلَاتِكَ وَلَا تُخَافِتْ بِهَا وَابْتَغِ بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ سَبِيْلًا‏(110)\nQOLID U’L LAAHA AWID U’R RAHMAAN, AYYAM MAA TAD-O’O FALAHUL ASMAAA-UL HUSNAA, WA LAA TAJHAR BE-SALAATEKA WA LAA TOKHAAFIT BEHAA WAB TAGHE BAYNA ZAALEKA SABEELAA.\nSay, ‘Invoke ‘‘Allah’’ or invoke ‘‘the All-beneficent.’’ Whichever [of His Names] you may invoke, to Him belong the Best Names.’ Be neither loud in your prayer, nor murmur it, but follow a middle course between these,\nوَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِى الْمُلْكِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلِىٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ وَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِيْرًا‏(111)\nWA QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE LAM YATTAKHIZ WALADANW WA LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL MULKE WA LAM YAKUL LAHU WALIYYUM MENAZ ZULLE WA KABBIRHO TAKBEERAA.\nand say, ‘All praise belongs to Allah, who has neither taken any son, nor has He any partner in sovereignty, nor has He any wali out of weakness,’ and magnify Him with a magnification [worthy of Him].",
  "merits": "Surah Bani Israaeel\nThere are 111 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a great reward will be accorded to those who recite this Surah and when they reach the verse about parents, they feel a sense of love and gentleness towards their parents.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah Bani Israeel every Thursday night, will not die before meeting Imam Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) and will be counted among his companions. Also, if a child is not able to speak or is delaying in his learning how to speak, he should be given the water of this Surah that has been written with saffron.\nIn the commentary of Safi it is written that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) told Imam Ali (a.s.) that the last two verses of this Surah are a protection and safety from theft. This Surah is also called Surah al-Isra’."
